    "q-133224": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133224",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{3}y+10xy, \\\\ {f}_{x}(2,1) & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3) \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y-0 \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{3}y+10xy) \\\\  & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a{x}^{2}y+10y & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${x}^{2}y,$ we get $b=\\frac{2}{3}a.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{x}(2,1)=14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,1) & =14 \\\\ a(2)^{2}(1)^{2}+5(1)^{2}-3 & =14 \\\\ 4a+2 & =14 \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $b=\\frac{2}{3}a=\\frac{2}{3}(3)=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-133224-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "a=3,\\,b=\\frac{3}{2}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"33\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"4\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-133224-b",
